{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "קדקדך", :translit "kodkodekha", :gloss "your crown of your head"} {:he "יולך ה' אותך ואת מלכך", :translit "yakkeh Hashem ot'kha ve'et mal'khekha", :gloss "YHWH will strike you and your king"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse words קדקד יהויקי[ם] read as allusion: קדקד (smiting) + יהויקי[ם] (Jehoiakim), though text appears corrupted."}], :frame {:text "Jehoiakim's death and denial of burial is described at Jeremiah 22:19 ('the burial of a donkey, dragged and cast out beyond the gates of Jerusalem') and Jeremiah 36:30 ('his dead body cast out to the heat by day and the frost by night'). The Second Temple era retelling in Josephus, Antiquities 10.97 states Nebuchadnezzar killed Jehoiakim and ordered his body cast unburied beyond the city walls. The midrashic tradition in Sifrei Devarim 287 explicitly connects the curses of Deuteronomy 28 to specific kings of Judah.", :sources ["Jeremiah 22:19" "Jeremiah 36:30" "Sifrei Devarim 287"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse words קדקד יהויקי[ם] read as allusion: קדקד (smiting) + יהויקי[ם] (Jehoiakim), though text appears corrupted.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:40:03.580377198Z", :model "glm-5.2"}